Exp No: 5 
Training a Pre-trained CNN Models using transfer learning with a  target dataset to create a trained model and to do the Multi-Class  Classification Using the Trained Model 
1. Aim 
To develop a deep learning pipeline for classifying images (OCT retinal scans and Fish diseases)  using Transfer Learning with pre-trained models (InceptionV3 and MobileNetV2) and to interpret  model decisions using Class Activation Mapping (Grad-CAM). 
2. Algorithm 
1. Data Preparation: 
o Initialize ImageDataGenerator to rescale pixel values to $[0, 1]$. 
o Load images from directories using flow_from_directory with specific target sizes  (e.g., $299 \times 299$). 
2. Model Construction (Transfer Learning): 
o Load a pre-trained base model (e.g., InceptionV3) with weights from ImageNet. o Exclude the top (fully connected) layers. 
o Add new global pooling and dense layers specific to the new dataset. 
o Freeze the base model layers to prevent weight updates during initial training. 3. Training & Evaluation: 
o Compile the model with an optimizer (Adam) and loss function (Categorical Cross Entropy). 
o Train on the new dataset and plot history for accuracy and loss. 
4. Performance Analysis: 
o Generate a Confusion Matrix to visualize true vs. predicted classifications across  multiple categories (e.g., "Red Disease", "Healthy Fish"). 
5. Interpretability (Grad-CAM): 
o Extract the output of the final convolutional layer. 
o Compute the gradient of the predicted class with respect to the feature maps. 
o Generate a heatmap representing "important" regions in the image and superimpose it  on the original image.
3. Implementation Summary 
import keras 
from keras.preprocessing.image import ImageDataGenerator  
from keras.applications.inception_v3 import InceptionV3  
from keras.layers import Dense, GlobalAveragePooling2D  
from keras.models import Model 
from keras import optimizers  
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt 
%matplotlib inline 
train_datagen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)  
test_datagen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)  
train_dir = '../OCT2017/train/' 
test_dir = '../OCT2017/test/' 
train_generator = train_datagen.flow_from_directory(train_dir, target_size=(299, 299), \ batch_size=128, class_mode='categorical')  
test_generator = test_datagen.flow_from_directory(test_dir, target_size=(299, 299), \ batch_size=128, class_mode='categorical') 
# create the base pre-trained model 
base_model = InceptionV3(weights='imagenet', include_top=False)  # Get the output layer from the pre-trained Inception V3 model 
x = base_model.output 
# Now, add new layers that will be trained with our data  
# These layers will be randomly initialized 
x = GlobalAveragePooling2D()(x)
x = Dense(64, activation='relu')(x) 
predictions = Dense(4, activation='softmax')(x) 
